class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">In person (Toronto)</th><th scope="col">Remote (anywhere)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Commission</td><td>Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%</td><td>Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source</td><td>Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>You choose</td><td>At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you</td></tr><tr><td>Every day</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach</td></tr><tr><td>Every month</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-remote-your-duties" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Remote: your duties</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remote duties</b> shows this month&#39;s touches against 400, today&#39;s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">For anything else press <b class="gd-ui">Log a touch</b>: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist ticks itself as the day&#39;s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under My availability choose this week or next, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a block</b> for each time you will be on, then <b class="gd-ui">Save the week</b>. Days already past stay as they were.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-my-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My sales</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Me</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b> tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press <b class="gd-ui">By month</b> for months, <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> for weeks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to you</td><td>A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else.</td></tr><tr><td>Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added</td><td>Counted on the day they happened.</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings confirmed, booked revenue</td><td>Counted on the day the booking was confirmed.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr><tr><td>Rental days (Sales)</td><td>The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month&#39;s tier applies to all of that month&#39;s rentals.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month&#39;s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owners-you-bring-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners you bring in</h2><p class="gd-p">Bring in car owners on <b class="gd-ui">My work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, card <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as &quot;sourced by&quot;, with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite an owner</b>: enter their name, email and phone, tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked me to send it</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the invitation</b>. They get an email with your link to apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Copy my owner link</b>: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Start an application</b>: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin&#39;s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>, and each car&#39;s tier (<b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b>). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span>: your owner link works for it too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The row of five figures follows your owners: <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Applied</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approved</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Car live</b> and <b class="gd-ui">First paid rental</b>. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task &quot;Unfinished owner application&quot; and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-ask-for-your-commission-on-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask for your commission on an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the owner&#39;s row press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a commission</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A flat amount</b> and type it, or <b class="gd-ui">A percent</b>: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company&#39;s share of their cars&#39; rentals, or their cars&#39; rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send to an Admin</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While it waits you can press <b class="gd-ui">Change my request</b>. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approved as</th><th scope="col">When it is earned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A flat amount</td><td>Once, at the owner&#39;s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full</td></tr><tr><td>A percent</td><td>On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars&#39; own cars, a partner&#39;s, a shareholder&#39;s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-buyer-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Buyer leads</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b>: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours, then call them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do &quot;Expired offer: win the renter back&quot; (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter&#39;s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Reopen offer</b> on an expired booking (or the <b class="gd-ui">Expired</b> filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 24 hours unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. &quot;Renter wants expired offer reopened&quot; To dos come from the renter&#39;s own button. The offer screens block <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> with <b class="gd-ui">Pickup time has passed: update it</b> until the pickup is moved.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-leads-and-claims" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Leads and claims</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Claim</b> on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or <b class="gd-ui">Note</b>) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Outcome</b>: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or <b class="gd-ui">Mark handled</b> when there is nothing more to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t finish? Press <b class="gd-ui">Unclaim</b> so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under <b class="gd-ui">My leads</b>: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-the-person-behind-the-lead-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The person behind the lead (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">The person</b> on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. <b class="gd-ui">Signals</b> lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.</p><p class="gd-p">When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show <b class="gd-ui">Assigned to you by an Admin</b>, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-call-minutes-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call minutes (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your home shows <b class="gd-ui">My call minutes</b>: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-get-a-renter-ready-for-the-pickup-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Payment</b>: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The offer</b>: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">ID and coverage</b>: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Drivers and agreement</b>: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Name change asked for</b>: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The booking page shows <b class="gd-ui">Ready for the rental</b>: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-the-prepare-checklist-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Prepare checklist (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking with add-ons, <b class="gd-ui">Prepare for the pickup</b> shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-rebooking-intent-and-offers-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A returning renter&#39;s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.</li><li>Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.</li><li>Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.</li><li>Prices stay between the owner&#39;s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.</li><li>Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).</li><li>Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-a-lead-customer-service-is-handling-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead customer service is handling (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-a-request-that-did-not-go-through-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request that did not go through (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A <b class="gd-ui">Request did not go through</b> To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-a-lead-s-phone-number-release-46" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead&#39;s phone number (release 46)</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> still reach the person through the business number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to show the number</b>. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says <b class="gd-ui">Number shown by an Admin</b>: the full number, with a call link and <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. Every other lead stays hidden.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
-- GUIDES 2871 END
